## Box 3|Examples for multifunctional efficiencies
The importance of the interplay of multifunctionality and simplicity of nanocarriers for drug delivery and therapeutic applications is exhibited in Box 1.For a better tangibility of this concept, the term ‘multifunctional efficiency (MFE)is introduced in Box 2. In this Box,we calculate the MFE for four specific examples discussed within this Perspective:
Fu et al. synthetized Mn-Zr metal-organic framework nanoparticles (MOF NPs)using a one-pot synthesis containing 3 building units (BUs), Mn- and Zrmetal salts as precursors for the inorganic building unit (IBU), as well as the organic building unit (OBU).75 Further surface coating was obtained using 1 process step (PRS)with 2 BUs, N-Hydroxysuccinimide and ${\mathrm{NH}}_{2}–\mathrm{PEG}–{\mathrm{NH}}_{2}$ Thus,this multifunctional NP was synthesized using 5 BUs, resulting in 3 functional units (FUs) in 2 PRSs, giving a MFE of 0.9, which can be described as a good degree of MFE. The functionalities are porosity exploited for microwave thermal therapy (MTT), Mn-doping used for microwave dynamic therapy (MDT), as well as the surface coating for colloidal stability and biocompatibility.
Chen et al. obtained functional NPs used for positron emission tomography (PET) imaging using 3 PRSs.78 The first PRS was used for the synthesis of the $^{89}\mathrm{Zr}$ MOF using3BUs,giving2FUs.1FU,thePET-imaging modalitywas induced by the radioactive IBU. Drug loading into the porous MOF in a second PRS resulted in the second FU. The third PRS uses 1 BU and results in 1 FU in form of a surface coating. In all, 5 BUs were used to achieve 3 FUs in 3 PRSs, which gives a MFE of 0.6. Although this NP possesses a comparably high functionality, the production process is complex, which decreases the MFE.
Zhuang et al. synthesized $\mathrm{Fe}_{3}\mathrm{O}_{4}@_{\ell}$ drug-encapsulated ZIF-8 core-shell NPs in a 1 PRS reaction containing 3 BUs giving 3 FUs.98 Besides the drug loading functionality, these particles possess colloidal stability without further surface modifications, and the core-shell structure enables selective localization within the body through external magnetic fields. This results in an extraordinarily high MFE of 3.
Liu et al. used a convenient one-pot synthesis containing 2 BUs to achieve NPs containing 2 FUs exploited for RT and PDT.105 A second PRS using one additional BU was used for surface modification for elongated blood circulation half-life, thus giving another FU. In total, this synthesis contained 2 PRSs, using 3 BUs and providing 3 FUs. This gives a MFE of 1.5. Further hypothetical loading of these particles with an active agent in one of the two PRSs would enable the MFE to improve to 2.
